  "reviews": {
    "P58fTC6d3_M": {
      "result": "verified_selected_lines",
      "notes": "Six branches begin after Ra6+ at 14s, with all seven pieces reconstructed. Ba3/Rxa3/Kb2 avoids the immediate Rf6 blockade and enables the king walk. Taking Ra2 gives a bishop fork and draw; taking Rg4 reaches a drawn pawn ending. After Kh6, Kxg6/Bxf5/Kf6 instead preserves a win. Ne7 before fxg8=Q/Bxg8 produces actual Ng6 mate. Immediate capture-promotion instead draws. Every encoded step is exact-checked; Rg4 is correctly written with check.",
