    "Rb8rgsHOeZY": {
      "result": "verified_selected_lines",
      "notes": "Four branches begin after Kxc6 at 43s, with White Ka6/Bg5/c2/d2 against Kc6/a3/d4. Bf6/Kd5/d3/a2/c4 checks both en passant and Kc5 defenses. Quiet Kb7 turns a1=Q into actual Be7 mate; an independent king retreat allows Bxd4. Premature Bxd4 loses the bishop and the exact ending. This is a closely related version of Most Majestic Game (zpX6pvMJhto), whose bishop starts on h4 rather than g5; both reach the same Bf6 core. The earlier eight-piece knight sacrifice remains context. The later caption A3 is corrected to the visually supported d3.",
